IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `tprai-types`

-- Third Parties (Rights against Insurers) Act 2010 (UK) — GOAL 1: TRANSFER
-- OF RIGHTS (ss 1, 4-7, 15, 16, Sch 3).
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/ukpga-2010-10.txt.

§ `Goal 1 — transfer of rights`

-- s 1(1) "This section applies if— (a) a relevant person incurs a liability
-- against which that person is insured under a contract of insurance, or (b)
-- a person who is subject to such a liability becomes a relevant person."
-- Route (a): already a relevant person when the liability is incurred
-- (including the same day); route (b): liable first.
@ref s 1(1)(a)
GIVEN t IS A `Transfer facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `route (a) applies to` t IF
    t's `became a relevant person on` AT MOST t's `the liability was incurred on`

-- ss 4(4), 5(1): a debt relief order, or dying insolvent, makes a person a
-- relevant person "for the purposes of section 1(1)(b) only".
-- s 6(5) "A body within subsection (1) is not a relevant person in relation
-- to a liability that is transferred to another body by the order"; (6) the
-- rights transfer "only to a person on whom the compromise or arrangement is
-- binding". s 6A(2): not if the body is treated as no longer dissolved; (3):
-- a partnership only if it is a body corporate.
@ref ss 1(1), 4(4), 5(1), 6(5)-(6), 6A
GIVEN t IS A `Transfer facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the event makes a relevant person for this transfer in` t IF
    CONSIDER t's `the event`
    WHEN `an insolvency event` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a debt relief order` THEN NOT (`route (a) applies to` t)
    WHEN `died insolvent` THEN NOT (`route (a) applies to` t)
    WHEN `a sanctioned compromise or arrangement` transferredAway binds THEN
        (NOT transferredAway) AND binds
    WHEN `dissolved` restored partnership THEN
        (NOT restored) AND (NOT partnership)
    WHEN `none` THEN FALSE

-- s 1(2) "The rights of the relevant person under the contract against the
-- insurer in respect of the liability are transferred to and vest in the
-- person to whom the liability is or was incurred (the “third party”)."
-- s 15: not where the liability is itself an insurer's liability under a
-- contract of insurance. s 16: voluntarily incurred liabilities count. Sch 3
-- para 3: where the 1930 Act still applies, this Act does not.
@ref ss 1(1)-(2), 4-7, 15, 16, Sch 3 paras 1, 3
@export Whether the insured's rights against its insurer in respect of a liability are transferred to the third party under s 1 of the Third Parties (Rights against Insurers) Act 2010 (UK): the insured is insured against the liability and is (or becomes) a relevant person under ss 4-7 (a debt relief order or death insolvent only where the liability came first; a sanctioned arrangement only where the liability stays with the body and binds the third party; a dissolved body unless restored, or a partnership that is not a body corporate), not reinsurance (s 15), and not a case still under the 1930 Act. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN t IS A `Transfer facts`  @desc The relevant-person event and its date, the date the liability was incurred, whether it is insured, reinsurance, and the 1930 Act case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the rights are transferred under` t IF
        t's `insured against the liability`
    AND `the event makes a relevant person for this transfer in` t
    AND NOT (t's `the liability is an insurer's liability under a contract of insurance`)
    AND NOT (t's `the 1930 Act still applies`)
